# Runtime artefacts — written by the running service, never source.
#
# The PID file in particular was tracked: it changes on every restart, and a
# committed value naming a process that is not this service is worse than no
# file at all (anything doing `kill $(cat …pid)` would signal the wrong one).
# It also blocked `git pull` for anyone whose service was running, because the
# incoming version would have overwritten their live one.
*.pid
logs/
.env
